1
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:02,910
Fear.

2
00:00:02,993 --> 00:00:04,120
Glorious fear.

3
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:08,240
It's a natural emotion
present in all animals.

4
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:10,720
Now I'm curious.

5
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:13,880
Tell me, what do you think causes fear?

6
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:19,580
There is the kind of fear
born of animal instincts.

7
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:24,920
And the kind of fear born of a
rational mind that terrorizes humans.

8
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:26,450
Namely,

9
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:30,397
when you encounter a foe stronger
than yourself and realize

10
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:33,920
you have no way of fighting
back against the unknown,

11
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:39,397
your helplessness begins
to sink in and evokes

12
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:43,260
inside of you a terrible
and paralyzing fear.

13
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:50,420
When you are faced with such fear,

14
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,188
you have a number of options
before you from which to choose.

15
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:59,320
You might struggle, resist,
flee, accept, or freeze.

16
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:05,120
But upon meeting Lord Dio, a
new unexpected reaction arises.

17
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:06,920
You feel joy!

18
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:12,180
How do you think most people
act once they feel joy and fear?

19
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:14,540
It's an interesting experience.

20
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:20,017
Our friend is currently on the plane
that Joestar and the others have boarded.

21
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:21,820
He'll greet them accordingly,

22
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:24,817
and they will find it
utterly impossible to

23
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:28,000
reach their final
destination in one piece.

24
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:08,900
A rhino beetle?

25
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:12,320
No, it's a stag beetle.

26
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:15,100
Hey, Avdol, is that a stand?

27
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:18,137
Are we already encountering
another stand user?

28
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:19,197
It's possible.

29
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:23,400
This could be a stem that takes
the shape of an insect. What the?

30
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,900
It hid in the shadow of the seats.

31
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:27,250
Damn.

32
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,795
It could be anywhere.

33
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:35,510
Jojo!

34
00:02:35,593 --> 00:02:36,497
It's next to your head!

35
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:37,698
Look to your right!

36
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:56,400
Let's go.

37
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:39,697
I'll see you

38
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:46,537
next

39
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:47,600
time.

40
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:52,280
It's time to go!

41
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:21,117
Sit tight, I'll take care of it.

42
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,540
Be extremely careful.

43
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:25,797
I've heard that there is a
user of an insect stand that

44
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:29,017
likes to rip out the tongues
of his victims before they die.

45
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:30,060
Star Platinum!

46
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,200
It dodged you.

47
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:36,900
I, I can't believe it.

48
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:38,777
It's faster than Star Platinum,

49
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:42,237
a stand that has the speed and
precision to grab a flying bullet.

50
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:44,137
Then there's no doubt about it.

51
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:47,020
That bug can only be a stand. Where is he?

52
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,278
Where is he hiding?

53
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:50,377
Where's the one who's controlling it?

54
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:51,636
We need to find him.

55
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:53,866
He's getting ready to attack.

56
00:04:57,660 --> 00:04:58,640
No, damn it.

57
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:01,170
Jotaro!

58
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:12,977
Star Platinum stopped it with its
teeth just in the nick of time.

59
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:14,100
Just as I feared.

60
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:16,773
It's going after Jotaro's Stan's tongue.

61
00:05:16,940 --> 00:05:17,780
It's him.

62
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:20,569
Represented by the
Tower Card of the Tarot.

63
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:25,747
Symbolizing Calamity and the interruption
of a journey, this stand is called...

64
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:29,220
Tower of Grey!

65
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:34,417
Tower of Grey is responsible
for countless mass murders,

66
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:36,817
which he made to look like
unfortunate accidents.

67
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:39,157
The plane crash last year in England that

68
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:41,757
caused over 300 deaths
was likely his work.

69
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:44,237
And how many more have
there been over the years?

70
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:47,555
I'd heard rumors, but to
think he's teamed up with Dio!

71
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,310
Hurrah!

72
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:57,920
It dodged that attack too?

73
00:05:58,200 --> 00:06:02,906
Not just from the single hand, but it
also dodged a two-fisted barrage of blows.

74
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:04,940
It's so fast!

75
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:10,457
Even if you had ten guns to shoot
bullets from one centimeter away,

76
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:12,917
they would not be able to touch my stand.

77
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,297
Not that you could kill a
stand with a gun anyways,

78
00:06:15,380 --> 00:06:18,792
You're all going to die with
the rest of these Wheatlings!

79
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:21,840
He has to be on this plane with us.

80
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:23,380
Who is it?

81
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:26,280
Who is the one controlling the stand?

82
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,780
Which one of the passengers is he?

83
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:36,040
If we can track him
down, we can squash him!

84
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:39,120
He disappeared again.

85
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:46,620
heads up it's over there now

86
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:55,160
what's it planning to do no it can't be

87
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:06,900
bingo got their tongues
now for the best part

88
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:16,090
Massacre!

89
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,580
Its definition?

90
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:19,260
To kill everyone!

91
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:22,660
No, it actually did it! Fine!

92
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:25,200
I'll burn that damn bug alive!

93
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:27,420
Go Magicians Red!

94
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:29,710
Avdol!

95
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,294
Just hold on a second!

96
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:38,980
It's so damn noisy on this flight.

97
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:42,440
What's with all the ruckus? Be careful!

98
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:44,701
Might as well go to the bathroom.

99
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:49,760
Why is this wet?

100
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,580
What's with all this slimy stuff?

101
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:55,570
Yes.

102
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,270
Blood!

103
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,360
This is blood!

104
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:04,130
Atum!

105
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:08,997
We have to defeat it before the
other passengers start to panic.

106
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,845
Easier said than done, though.

107
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:13,270
Mr. Avdol,

108
00:08:13,353 --> 00:08:15,417
using an active stand
like your magician's red

109
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:18,097
inside an airborne plane
could make it explode,

110
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:19,117
killing all of us.

111
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:23,657
Jojo, if your power were to rip a hole
in the fuselage, it'd be a catastrophe.

112
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:26,220
This calls for a quiet and discreet stand.

113
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:29,997
My hierophant green is most
suited to defeating it.

114
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:32,256
Let me take care of the pest control.

115
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:38,300
I've heard all about you from Lord Dio.

116
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,260
Don't bother.

117
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:43,800
You think you have silence on your side.

118
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:47,520
But your stand cannot
keep up with my speed.

119
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,000
You sure about that?

120
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,620
Emerald Splash! Splash!

121
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:01,660
Emerald splash again!

122
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:09,177
You seem to think you can hit
me if you fire enough shots,

123
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:11,240
but you haven't hit me at all.

124
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:13,980
Not good.

125
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:16,673
It's dodging everything he throws at it.

126
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:21,370
Kacueing!

127
00:09:24,260 --> 00:09:26,460
I'm just too fast for you.

128
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:29,740
You're way too slow to get a bingo.

129
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:31,960
And kakyoin,

130
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,456
with my next attack,

131
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:37,317
I'll stab your Stan's tongue with
this tower needle and rip it out.

132
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:38,820
Won't that be fun?

133
00:09:41,020 --> 00:09:42,140
Emerald Splash!

134
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:43,860
Don't you get it?

135
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,100
Damn, impossible.

136
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,977
How can he win if his attacks
don't find their mark?

137
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:54,740
You'll go mad from the pain
once this rips its tongue out.

138
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:56,960
How exquisite!

139
00:09:57,880 --> 00:09:58,710
Sad right.

140
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:02,116
If its tongue's ripped out,
I'll go mad from the pain?

141
00:10:02,420 --> 00:10:05,140
My hierophant green
will go mad, all right.

142
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:10,780
What? Ow!

143
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:14,100
If it rips you apart, it'll go mad.

144
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:16,100
From pure joy.

145
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:25,757
His appendages had already
slipped beneath the seats.

146
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:28,840
I just needed enough time
to set up my little trap.

147
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:33,640
You didn't realize I was using my
emerald splash to keep you in one spot?

148
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:44,260
What the...?

149
00:10:46,860 --> 00:10:49,680
So that geezer was the
user all along, huh?

150
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:53,000
Um, guess I should have expected as much.

151
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:56,060
A repulsive stand usually
has a repulsive user.

152
00:11:00,340 --> 00:11:01,575
Well, that's strange.

153
00:11:01,740 --> 00:11:05,328
It doesn't look like he had
Dio's flesh butt in his forehead.

154
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:07,600
Tower of Grey was always evil.

155
00:11:08,060 --> 00:11:11,057
He killed Turris by the
hundreds and got paid for it.

156
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:14,437
He'd make it look like an accident
and got away with it every time.

157
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:19,940
I'm sure Tio was able to use him because
he was easily bought and blinded by greed

158
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:26,617
Something's wrong.

159
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:28,137
It could be my imagination,

160
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:31,867
but I get the feeling this plane
isn't flying straight anymore

161
00:11:35,940 --> 00:11:37,897
It's crooked no doubt about it.

162
00:11:37,980 --> 00:11:39,640
Eh, it can't be

163
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:46,377
Sorry, sir, you can't be up here.

164
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:49,217
The cockpit is up ahead, so
passengers may not enter.

165
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:50,130
I know that!

166
00:11:51,220 --> 00:11:52,050
Sir, wait!

167
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,500
He's so handsome!

168
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:03,380
Move it, bitch!

169
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:05,660
What a shock!

170
00:12:06,340 --> 00:12:08,340
Whoa there. Sorry, ladies.

171
00:12:08,840 --> 00:12:12,097
His disrespectful behavior
towards you two is incorrigible.

172
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:14,415
But we have an emergency on our hands.

173
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:20,657
please forgive him for
me okay damn it this

174
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:25,797
is horrible we've been had their tongues

175
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:28,817
have been ripped out that rhino bastard he

176
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:31,488
killed the pilots before
we knew he was here

177
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:39,840
hmm we're losing altitude fast the
autopilot's been destroyed as well

178
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:43,850
Damn it!

179
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:45,195
We're going to crash!

180
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:50,070
What?

181
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:59,300
My Stand at the Tower card would signify
horrible accidents and the end of journey.

182
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:03,257
I'll keep you from Lord Dio
if it's the last thing I do.

183
00:13:03,340 --> 00:13:08,377
Even if you manage to survive the crash,
you're still 10,000 kilometers from Egypt.

184
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:12,940
Those who swore loyalty to Lord
Dio will pursue you relentlessly.

185
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:15,281
You don't stand a chance in hell.

186
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:20,521
There are stands in this world with powers
that defy the very limits of imagination.

187
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:24,554
Lord Dio's power is the one
that rules over all of them.

188
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:29,660
He is the master of stands, reigning
over the world like a god among mortals.

189
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:32,057
There's no way you'll reach them alive.

190
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:35,100
You bastards won't even see Egypt!

191
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,860
Your deaths will be swift and painful!

192
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:45,622
You're definitely professionals.

193
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:47,977
Good thing you didn't scream.

194
00:13:48,060 --> 00:13:50,178
That annoys me all to freaking hell.

195
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:52,280
Now, I've got a request.

196
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:56,557
This heap's gonna hit water, and
this old man's gonna land her there.

197
00:13:56,640 --> 00:14:01,228
Go put life jackets on the other passengers,
and make sure they're buckled up.

198
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:02,970
Yes, sir.

199
00:14:03,053 --> 00:14:04,720
You've got this? Hmm.

200
00:14:05,460 --> 00:14:09,540
I have some experience with prop
planes, but this... Prop planes?

201
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:13,860
But, Jotaro, this will make
three plane crashes for me.

202
00:14:14,140 --> 00:14:17,877
Have you ever heard of someone
being in a plane crash three times?

203
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:20,140
Let alone surviving each one?

204
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:25,040
That settles it.

205
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:28,669
I'm never riding in a
plane with you again.

206
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:51,220
The plane landed 35 kilometers
off the coast of Hong Kong.

207
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:55,457
Jotaro and the others had no
choice but to head to the city.

208
00:14:55,540 --> 00:14:57,658
South of Hong Kong near Lama Island.

209
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,722
Rescue efforts are now underway.

210
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:01,800
Hong Kong!

211
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:05,420
Hong Kong Island, Kowloon,
the New Territories.

212
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:09,160
With more than 235 individual
islands in the area,

213
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:14,167
its breathtaking nightscape is known the
world over as the Million Dollar View.

214
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:15,960
Yeah, no problem.

215
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:17,360
That'll be fine.

216
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:21,112
Please make sure the only ones
aboard are us and the crew.

217
00:15:21,220 --> 00:15:22,050
Right.

218
00:15:22,260 --> 00:15:25,277
There's been enough collateral
damage because of us.

219
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:26,897
By the way...

220
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:28,400
Hey, big guy!

221
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:32,457
You guys aren't from around here, are you?

222
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:33,717
Want some rice porridge?

223
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:36,537
Can't come to Hong Kong and I try
our rice porridge and dim sum?

224
00:15:36,620 --> 00:15:38,208
We have some hot cola, too!

225
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:40,540
Rice porridge, not bad.

226
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:45,977
Did you know, Jojo, unlike in Japan, rice
porridge is a staple food in Hong Kong.

227
00:15:46,060 --> 00:15:47,884
To some, it's quite a delicacy.

228
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:51,857
One bowl, the popular way with pork
and century egg, if you have it.

229
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:52,920
Coming right up!

230
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:54,820
In that case, I'll have...

231
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,190
Hey!

232
00:15:56,273 --> 00:15:57,103
What?

233
00:15:57,186 --> 00:15:58,016
You boys think we have time to eat?

234
00:15:58,099 --> 00:15:59,257
We're going to my old favorite.

235
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:01,177
You can wait to stuff your faces there.

236
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:03,017
Hey, you dandy guy over there.

237
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:06,900
I know you'd be interested in
some Hong Kong hot cola. Hot cola?

238
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:08,420
That's blasphemy.

239
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:10,457
Everyone knows it's supposed to be cold.

240
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:12,740
Old man, who were you just calling?

241
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,020
Oh, that.

242
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,077
I'll explain when we
get to the restaurant.

243
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:17,990
Be patient.

244
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,797
We need to work out a plan that'll get us

245
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,157
to Egypt as safely and
quickly as possible.

246
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:26,257
More users are bound to come after
us, and that could cost lives.

247
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:28,520
Right. A plan.

248
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:30,020
I agree with you.

249
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:34,297
We can't allow any more innocent civilians
to be hurt because of our failure.

250
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:37,380
The quickest way would be
by plane, but that's out.

251
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:39,250
Indeed.

252
00:16:39,333 --> 00:16:42,760
It's now become completely
impossible for us to fly to Egypt.

253
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:44,310
You see,

254
00:16:44,460 --> 00:16:48,397
if we encounter a STAN user like
the last one on a commercial flight,

255
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:49,880
we'll cause a disaster.

256
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:53,317
One that will harm many people
and might kill many more.

257
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:57,700
With that in mind, we'll have to
get to Egypt by either land or sea.

258
